#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:149
msgid "A gradual start for new and returning workers"
msgstr "Un comienzo gradual para trabajadores nuevos y que regresan"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:150
msgid ""
"Bodies take about a week to adjust to heat. New workers spend only part of "
"the hot hours in the heat at first, following NIOSH guidance. Only days at "
"Caution or above count. After a week or more away from hot work, the "
"returning schedule starts again."
msgstr ""
"El cuerpo tarda alrededor de una semana en acostumbrarse al calor. Al "
"principio, los trabajadores nuevos pasan solo una parte de las horas de "
"calor en el calor, según las recomendaciones de NIOSH. Solo cuentan los días"
" con nivel de Precaución o más. Después de una semana o más sin trabajar con"
" calor, se vuelve a empezar el plan para quienes regresan."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:153
msgid "New to hot work"
msgstr "Nuevo en el trabajo con calor"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:154
#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:160
#: crews/templates/crews/plan_page.html:9
msgid "Day"
msgstr "Día"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:154
#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:160
msgid "Share of hot hours"
msgstr "Parte de las horas de calor"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:159
msgid "Experienced, new to the crew or returning"
msgstr "Con experiencia, nuevo en la cuadrilla o que regresa"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:166
msgid "Water, rest and shade"
msgstr "Agua, descanso y sombra"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:168
msgid ""
"Cool drinking water close to the work, enough for 1 quart per worker per "
"hour. Drink 1 cup every 15–20 minutes, even when not thirsty."
msgstr ""
"Agua fresca para tomar cerca del trabajo, suficiente para 1 cuarto de galón "
"por trabajador por hora. Tome 1 vaso cada 15 a 20 minutos, aunque no tenga "
"sed."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:169
msgid ""
"Shade big enough for everyone on break to sit at the same time, as close to "
"the work as possible."
msgstr ""
"Sombra suficiente para que todos los que descansan se sienten al mismo "
"tiempo, lo más cerca posible del trabajo."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:170
msgid ""
"Anyone may take a rest in shade at any time to prevent overheating. Rest at "
"least 5 minutes and until they feel better."
msgstr ""
"Cualquiera puede descansar a la sombra en cualquier momento para no "
"sobrecalentarse. Descanse al menos 5 minutos y hasta sentirse mejor."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:171
msgid ""
"Buddies check on each other at the times above. Reply to Shadebreak texts: 1"
" = OK, 2 = needs help."
msgstr ""
"Los compañeros se revisan entre sí a las horas indicadas. Responda a los "
"mensajes de Shadebreak: 1 = bien, 2 = necesita ayuda."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:174
msgid "Warning signs and first aid"
msgstr "Señales de alerta y primeros auxilios"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:177
msgid "Heat exhaustion"
msgstr "Agotamiento por calor"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:178
msgid ""
"Heavy sweating, cool pale clammy skin, fast weak pulse, nausea or vomiting, "
"muscle cramps, tiredness or weakness, dizziness, headache, fainting."
msgstr ""
"Sudor abundante, piel fría, pálida y húmeda, pulso rápido y débil, náuseas o"
" vómito, calambres, cansancio o debilidad, mareo, dolor de cabeza, desmayo."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:180
msgid "Stop work. Move to shade or a cool place."
msgstr "Pare de trabajar. Vaya a la sombra o a un lugar fresco."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:181
msgid "Loosen clothing. Cool with wet cloths and fanning."
msgstr "Afloje la ropa. Refresque con trapos mojados y abanicando."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:182
msgid "Sip cool water."
msgstr "Tome agua fresca a sorbos."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:183
msgid ""
"Get medical help if they vomit, get worse, or are not better within an hour."
" Do not leave them alone."
msgstr ""
"Busque atención médica si vomita, empeora o no mejora en una hora. No lo "
"deje solo."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:187
msgid "Heat stroke: a medical emergency"
msgstr "Golpe de calor: una emergencia médica"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:188
msgid ""
"Confusion, slurred speech, acting strange, fainting or seizures, very high "
"body temperature, hot red skin that may be dry or damp."
msgstr ""
"Confusión, habla arrastrada, comportamiento extraño, desmayo o convulsiones,"
" temperatura del cuerpo muy alta, piel caliente y roja que puede estar seca "
"o húmeda."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:190
#, python-format
msgid "Call %(number)s now."
msgstr "Llame al %(number)s ahora."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:191
msgid ""
"Cool them right away: cold water or ice on the body, ice-water immersion if "
"available, wet towels and fanning."
msgstr ""
"Enfríe a la persona de inmediato: agua fría o hielo en el cuerpo, inmersión "
"en agua con hielo si hay, toallas mojadas y abanicar."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:192
msgid ""
"Stay with them. Do not give drinks if they are confused or not fully awake."
msgstr ""
"Quédese con la persona. No le dé de beber si está confundida o no está bien "
"despierta."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:193
msgid "Send someone to meet the ambulance and guide it in."
msgstr "Mande a alguien a recibir a la ambulancia y guiarla."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:198
msgid "In an emergency"
msgstr "En una emergencia"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:200
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Call %(number)s. Say: \"Heat emergency,\" the site address and the closest "
"cross street."
msgstr ""
"Llame al %(number)s. Diga: \"Emergencia por calor\", la dirección de la obra"
" y la calle cercana que la cruza."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:201
msgid ""
"Start cooling the worker while you wait. Keep cooling until help arrives."
msgstr ""
"Empiece a enfriar al trabajador mientras espera. Siga enfriando hasta que "
"llegue la ayuda."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:202
msgid "the crew lead"
msgstr "el jefe de cuadrilla"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:202
#, python-format
msgid "Tell %(name)s right away."
msgstr "Avise de inmediato a %(name)s."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:205
msgid "Sign-off"
msgstr "Firmas"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:206
msgid ""
"I received this plan and was trained on heat illness: signs, first aid, "
"water, rest, shade and my right to stop and cool down."
msgstr ""
"Recibí este plan y me capacitaron sobre las enfermedades por calor: señales,"
" primeros auxilios, agua, descanso, sombra y mi derecho a parar y "
"refrescarme."

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:208
msgid "Signature"
msgstr "Firma"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:208
msgid "Date"
msgstr "Fecha"

#: crews/templates/crews/plan/heat_plan.html:215
msgid ""
"Sources: NIOSH Criteria for a Recommended Standard, Occupational Exposure to"
" Heat and Hot Environments (2016); ACGIH heat stress TLV and action limit as"
" reproduced in the OSHA Technical Manual; National Weather Service heat "
"index; WBGT estimated with the Liljegren method (thermofeel). Breaks follow "
"the 2024 proposed OSHA heat rule's triggers; check current OSHA and state "
"rules that apply to you."
msgstr ""
"Fuentes: NIOSH, Criterios para una norma recomendada sobre exposición "
"ocupacional al calor (2016); TLV y límite de acción de ACGIH para estrés por"
" calor, según el Manual Técnico de OSHA; índice de calor del Servicio "
"Meteorológico Nacional; WBGT estimado con el método de Liljegren "
"(thermofeel). Los descansos siguen los umbrales de la norma de calor "
"propuesta por OSHA en 2024; revise las normas actuales de OSHA y de su "
"estado que le apliquen."

